{"step_index":819,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T22:15:42Z","thinking":"**Implementing Expression Lowering**\n\nI'm now diving into `ops/runtime/sovrac.zig`. The current focus is the full implementation of AST expression lowering, targeting ARM64 instruction emission. I'm starting with `add`, `sub`, `mul`, and `sdiv`, as well as control flow instructions. I am starting by implementing function calls (via `bl _sovrac_gate_sanitizer`) and comparison and branching instructions. I will carefully move forward.\n\n\n**Developing Full Code Generation**\n\nI'm now integrating token lexing for arithmetic and control flow constructs in `sovrac.zig`. I am focusing on building statement IR and developing dynamic ARM64 CodeGen. I'm aiming to fully implement AST lowering, with arithmetic and control flow, which will be the heart of my approach!\n\n\n**Refining Lexical Analysis**\n\nI've been working on refining the lexical analysis, focusing on token recognition in `sovrac.zig`. I am implementing string literals, number literals, and comparison operators. I am handling special characters within strings and defining individual tokens for operators and delimiters. I'm making good progress.\n\n\n**Expanding Token Recognition**\n\nI'm now focusing on expanding the token recognition in my lexer. I've added parsing for parentheses, braces, angle brackets and the '@' symbol, along with identifiers, including the `@invariant` keyword. Further keywords are added, such as `fn`, `val`, `candidate`, and `decision`. I am progressing steadily.\n\n\n**Adding Keyword and Data Types**\n\nI've been expanding the token definitions by implementing the keywords \"gate\", \"if\", \"else\", \"while\", and \"return\", as well as keywords related to specific data types and system functions such as \"SHM_RingBuffer\", \"HyperVector\", \"system.execute\", \"fs.write\", and \"net.send\" in `sovrac.zig`. I am also working on defining `DataType` and `VarSymbol` structs.\n\n\n**Defining Intermediate Representation**\n\nI'm now focused on defining the Intermediate Representation (IR) structures within the compiler. I'm working on `IRStatement`, `OpCode`, and related structs, including `CompilerEngine`. These structures will manage symbol tables and IR statements. I'm also implementing the compiler engine initialization and symbol lookup, as well as IR emission functionality. I'm progressing with the hypervector.\n\n\n**Analyzing Assignment Statements**\n\nI'm now focused on parsing assignment statements, especially those involving type declarations and initializations. I'm handling assignments with numeric literals, gate calls (for taint lifting), and variable assignments with optional arithmetic operations. I'm also implementing the handling of generic parameters, such as <ToolCall>. I am making good progress.\n\n\n**Implementing Control Flow and Sinks**\n\nI'm working on `while` loop parsing now, including handling the condition and loop body. I am emitting `WhileHead` and `WhileEnd` IR statements. I'm also implementing checks for security sinks (like `system.execute`, `fs.write`, `net.send`), ensuring that tainted variables aren't directly passed to these functions. Error handling is also underway.\n\n\n**Finalizing Code Generation**\n\nI've just completed the integration of native ARM64 machine assembly code generation within the compiler. I have successfully translated the Intermediate Representation (IR) statements into assembly code. I'm now verifying the correctness of the generated assembly for various arithmetic operations and constant assignments, and I am ensuring stack frame management and register usage are correct.\n\n\n**Generating ARM64 Assembly**\n\nI'm now generating ARM64 assembly code. Specifically, I've implemented subtraction and multiplication instruction emission. I'm focusing on arithmetic operations with register assignments, including loading operands from the stack and storing results. I have also completed implementing the `CallGate` instruction, and I'm generating code for the gate call with a `bl` instruction. I am now working on implementing while loop head instructions, with stack offsets for the conditional variable and comparisons.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Syscall Implementation**\n\nI've just added the implementation for system calls, specifically `CallSyscall`, which I have integrated into my ARM64 assembly code. I'm focusing on the `sys_write` syscall to handle standard output, and I've now integrated file I/O within the compiler. I've also implemented the \"loop end\" functionality, and I have completed function exit and stack cleanup. This concludes my work on the compiler's core functionality!\n\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"// SOVRA NATIVE COMPILER v3.0 (sovrac.zig)\n// Canonical Reference: Codified 2026-09-28 by Anthony & Maxx.\n// Mission: Fuses Security Properties (OWASP ASI-01, Capability Lattice) AND lowers AST expressions to ARM64 Machine Assembly (add, sub, mul, bl, cmp, b.eq, b).\n\nconst std = @import(\"std\");\nconst print = std.debug.print;\n\npub const TokenType = enum {\n    KwFn,\n    KwVal,\n    KwCandidate,\n    KwDecision,\n    KwGate,\n    KwInvariant,\n    KwShmRingBuffer,\n    KwHyperVector,\n    KwSystemExecute,\n    KwFsWrite,\n    KwNetSend,\n    KwIf,\n    KwElse,\n    KwWhile,\n    KwReturn,\n    Identifier,\n    Equals,\n    Colon,\n    Plus,\n    Minus,\n    Star,\n    Slash,\n    CmpEq,\n    CmpNe,\n    CmpLt,\n    CmpGt,\n    LParen,\n    RParen,\n    LBrace,\n    RBrace,\n    LAngle,\n    RAngle,\n    StringLit,\n    NumberLit,\n    Semicolon,\n    Eof,\n    Invalid,\n};\n\npub const Token = struct {\n    kind: TokenType,\n    text: []const u8,\n    line: usize,\n};\n\npub const Lexer = struct {\n    source: []const u8,\n    cursor: usize,\n    line: usize,\n\n    pub fn init(source: []const u8) Lexer {\n        return Lexer{\n            .source = source,\n            .cursor = 0,\n            .line = 1,\n        };\n    }\n\n    pub fn next_token(self: *Lexer) Token {\n        while (self.cursor < self.source.len) {\n            const c = self.source[self.cursor];\n\n            // Skip single-line comments\n            if (c == '/' and self.cursor + 1 < self.source.len and self.source[self.cursor + 1] == '/') {\n                while (self.cursor < self.source.len and self.source[self.cursor] != '\\n') {\n                    self.cursor += 1;\n                }\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            if (c == '\\n') {\n                self.line += 1;\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                continue;\n            }\n            if (c == ' ' or c == '\\t' or c == '\\r') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            // String literals\n            if (c == '\"') {\n                const start = self.cursor;\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                while (self.cursor < self.source.len and self.source[self.cursor] != '\"') {\n                    if (self.source[self.cursor] == '\\\\' and self.cursor + 1 < self.source.len) {\n                        self.cursor += 2;\n                    } else {\n                        self.cursor += 1;\n                    }\n                }\n                if (self.cursor < self.source.len) self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .StringLit, .text = self.source[start..self.cursor], .line = self.line };\n            }\n\n            // Numbers\n            if (std.ascii.isDigit(c)) {\n                const start = self.cursor;\n                while (self.cursor < self.source.len and std.ascii.isDigit(self.source[self.cursor])) {\n                    self.cursor += 1;\n                }\n                return Token{ .kind = .NumberLit, .text = self.source[start..self.cursor], .line = self.line };\n            }\n\n            if (c == '=' and self.cursor + 1 < self.source.len and self.source[self.cursor + 1] == '=') {\n                self.cursor += 2;\n                return Token{ .kind = .CmpEq, .text = \"==\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == '!' and self.cursor + 1 < self.source.len and self.source[self.cursor + 1] == '=') {\n                self.cursor += 2;\n                return Token{ .kind = .CmpNe, .text = \"!=\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == '=') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .Equals, .text = \"=\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == '+') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .Plus, .text = \"+\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == '-') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .Minus, .text = \"-\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == '*') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .Star, .text = \"*\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == '/') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .Slash, .text = \"/\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == ':') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .Colon, .text = \":\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == ';') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .Semicolon, .text = \";\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == '(') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .LParen, .text = \"(\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == ')') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .RParen, .text = \")\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == '{') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .LBrace, .text = \"{\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == '}') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .RBrace, .text = \"}\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == '<') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .LAngle, .text = \"<\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == '>') {\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                return Token{ .kind = .RAngle, .text = \">\", .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (c == '@') {\n                const start = self.cursor;\n                self.cursor += 1;\n                while (self.cursor < self.source.len and (std.ascii.isAlphanumeric(self.source[self.cursor]) or self.source[self.cursor] == '_')) {\n                    self.cursor += 1;\n                }\n                const text = self.source[start..self.cursor];\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"@invariant\")) {\n                    return Token{ .kind = .KwInvariant, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                }\n                return Token{ .kind = .Identifier, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n            }\n            if (std.ascii.isAlphabetic(c) or c == '_' or c == '.') {\n                const start = self.cursor;\n                while (self.cursor < self.source.len and (std.ascii.isAlphanumeric(self.source[self.cursor]) or self.source[self.cursor] == '_' or self.source[self.cursor] == '.')) {\n                    self.cursor += 1;\n                }\n                const text = self.source[start..self.cursor];\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"fn\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwFn, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"val\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwVal, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"candidate\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwCandidate, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"decision\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwDecision, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"gate\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwGate, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"if\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwIf, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"else\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwElse, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"while\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwWhile, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"return\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwReturn, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"SHM_RingBuffer\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwShmRingBuffer, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"HyperVector\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwHyperVector, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"system.execute\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwSystemExecute, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"fs.write\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwFsWrite, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                if (std.mem.eql(u8, text, \"net.send\")) return Token{ .kind = .KwNetSend, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n                return Token{ .kind = .Identifier, .text = text, .line = self.line };\n            }\n            self.cursor += 1;\n        }\n        return Token{ .kind = .Eof, .text = \"\", .line = self.line };\n    }\n};\n\npub const DataType = enum {\n    CandidateTainted,\n    DecisionCertified,\n    ShmRingBuffer,\n    HyperVector,\n    Integer64,\n    Unknown,\n};\n\npub const VarSymbol = struct {\n    name: []const u8,\n    type_kind: DataType,\n    is_tainted: bool,\n    stack_offset: usize,\n    line: usize,\n};\n\npub const OpCode = enum {\n    Add,\n    Sub,\n    Mul,\n    Div,\n    CallGate,\n    CallSyscall,\n    AssignConst,\n    AssignVar,\n    WhileHead,\n    WhileEnd,\n};\n\npub const IRStatement = struct {\n    op: OpCode,\n    dest: []const u8,\n    src1: []const u8,\n    src2: []const u8,\n    imm_val: i64,\n};\n\npub const CompilerEngine = struct {\n    symbols: [128]VarSymbol,\n    symbol_count: usize,\n    ir_statements: [256]IRStatement,\n    ir_count: usize,\n    has_error: bool,\n    ast_hypervector: [312]u32,\n\n    pub fn init() CompilerEngine {\n        var engine = CompilerEngine{\n            .symbols = undefined,\n            .symbol_count = 0,\n            .ir_statements = undefined,\n            .ir_count = 0,\n            .has_error = false,\n            .ast_hypervector = undefined,\n        };\n        for (0..312) |i| engine.ast_hypervector[i] = 0;\n        return engine;\n    }\n\n    pub fn find_symbol(self: *CompilerEngine, name: []const u8) ?*VarSymbol {\n        for (0..self.symbol_count) |i| {\n            if (std.mem.eql(u8, self.symbols[i].name, name)) {\n                return &self.symbols[i];\n            }\n        }\n        return null;\n    }\n\n    pub fn emit_ir(self: *CompilerEngine, stmt: IRStatement) void {\n        if (self.ir_count < 256) {\n            self.ir_statements[self.ir_count] = stmt;\n            self.ir_count += 1;\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub fn compile_source(self: *CompilerEngine, filename: []const u8, source: []const u8) bool {\n        print(\"\\n==========================================================\\n\", .{});\n        print(\" SOVRA NATIVE COMPILER v3.0 (sovrac) - COMPILING '{s}'\\n\", .{filename});\n        print(\"==========================================================\\n\", .{});\n\n        var lex = Lexer.init(source);\n        var tok = lex.next_token();\n\n        var hv_idx: usize = 0;\n\n        while (tok.kind != .Eof) {\n            for (tok.text) |byte| {\n                self.ast_hypervector[hv_idx % 312] ^= (@as(u32, byte) *% 1337);\n                hv_idx += 1;\n            }\n\n            if (tok.kind == .KwVal) {\n                // val <var_name> : <type> = <rhs> ;\n                const name_tok = lex.next_token(); // Variable Name\n                const var_name = name_tok.text;\n                const line = name_tok.line;\n\n                _ = lex.next_token(); // Colon :\n                const type_tok = lex.next_token(); // Type Name\n\n                var type_kind: DataType = .Unknown;\n                var is_tainted = false;\n\n                if (type_tok.kind == .KwCandidate) {\n                    type_kind = .CandidateTainted;\n                    is_tainted = true; // ALL candidates are TAINTED by default!\n                } else if (type_tok.kind == .KwDecision) {\n                    type_kind = .DecisionCertified;\n                    is_tainted = false; // Must be validated by gate\n                } else if (type_tok.kind == .KwShmRingBuffer) {\n                    type_kind = .ShmRingBuffer;\n                } else if (type_tok.kind == .KwHyperVector) {\n                    type_kind = .HyperVector;\n                } else if (type_tok.kind == .Identifier and std.mem.eql(u8, type_tok.text, \"i64\")) {\n                    type_kind = .Integer64;\n                }\n\n                // Generic parameters e.g. <ToolCall>\n                var next_t = lex.next_token();\n                if (next_t.kind == .LAngle) {\n                    _ = lex.next_token(); // inner type\n                    _ = lex.next_token(); // RAngle >\n                    next_t = lex.next_token();\n                }\n\n                if (next_t.kind == .Equals) {\n                    const rhs_first = lex.next_token();\n\n                    if (rhs_first.kind == .NumberLit) {\n                        const imm = std.fmt.parseInt(i64, rhs_first.text, 10) catch 0;\n                        self.emit_ir(IRStatement{\n                            .op = .AssignConst,\n                            .dest = var_name,\n                            .src1 = \"\",\n                            .src2 = \"\",\n                            .imm_val = imm,\n                        });\n                    } else if (rhs_first.kind == .KwGate) {\n                        // gate(...) block sanitizer: Lifts taint!\n                        i